  "key_findings": [
    "The bounded run observed 400 and 401 among DeepSeek's seven documented statuses.",
    "The server also returned 404, 405 and 415 for route, method and media-type failures; these are real HTTP results but are not listed on DeepSeek's seven-code quick-reference page.",
    "Invalid model, temperature, message shape and oversized user_id examples returned 400, not 422, in this run.",
    "No live response in this bounded matrix returned 422, so the article does not claim a universal 400-versus-422 boundary.",
    "A user_id containing a space was accepted once even though the current documentation requires a restricted regex. Production clients should continue to follow the documented contract.",
    "The 401 JSON error.code string was invalid_request_error, demonstrating that the JSON field is not the same thing as the numeric HTTP status.",
    "No observed response included Retry-After. Production code should honor the header when present, but must not assume DeepSeek always sends it."
  ],
